    {
      "name": "actual_weighted_numerator_and_pole_denominator",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "baseNumerator is n!^7 times both original finite products; baseU=X*(X+C n). The independent exact quotient-evaluation theorem identifies weightedNumerator.eval/polePolynomial.eval^9 with frozen actual weightedR. No abstract numerator or coefficient input replaces these constructions."
    },
    {
      "name": "all_nine_orders_and_9_minus_s_indexing",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "For every k<9, s=9-k lies in 1..9 and 9-(9-k)=k. Zero of all nine actual weightedLocalCoefficient values therefore gives precisely coefficients 0..8 zero of the genuine weightedClearedSeries. PowerSeries.X_pow_dvd_iff proves X^9 divisibility; multiplication by the actual denominator identity and Polynomial.coeff_coe transfer it to the shifted polynomial numerator."
    },
    {
      "name": "inverse_shift_and_actual_pole_factor_divisibility",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "weightedNumerator.comp(X-C j) is the actual shifted weighted numerator. Composing a divisibility witness with X+C j cancels the shift and transforms X^9 into (X+C j)^9. The sign and inverse order are correct; no coefficient or factor-divisibility hypothesis is added."
    },
    {
      "name": "pairwise_coprime_all_poles_and_full_ninth_power",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "Distinct natural a,b remain distinct in Q. The differences of roots -a,-b are nonzero units, giving coprime X+C a and X+C b and their ninth powers. Finset.prod_dvd_of_coprime across range(n+1), with j<=n obtained from membership, gives the full polePolynomial^9 dividing the actual weighted numerator."
    },
    {
      "name": "proper_degree_contradiction_handles_zero_correctly",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "The full denominator has degree 9(n+1), and the actual weighted numerator has degree at most 2n+2 natDegree W. The proof uses natDegree_le_of_dvd only under a temporary weightedNumerator!=0 hypothesis. Thus zero natDegree conventions cannot create a false divisibility comparison; the strict bound forces numerator=0."
    },
    {
      "name": "nonzero_base_and_nondegenerate_quadratic_cancel_to_W_zero",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "The actual base numerator is nonzero by nonzero n!^7 and nonzero linear factors, also for n=0. The actual baseU has degree 2 for every n. Polynomial.comp_eq_zero_iff leaves W=0 or a constant inner polynomial; the latter contradicts degree 2. This is genuine polynomial composition cancellation, with no assumed matrix injection."
    },
    {
      "name": "difference_proper_domain_and_actual_linearity",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "natDegree(W-V)<=max(natDegree W,natDegree V) makes the strict domain closed under differences when both W and V are proper; independent_difference_proper independently checks this. Polynomial sub_comp, polynomial-to-series subtraction, multiplication and coeff maps prove the actual coefficient difference identity. The zero kernel then gives W=V."
    },
    {
      "name": "Fin_n_plus_one_by_Fin_nine_subtype_array_is_complete",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "fullLocalCoefficientMap reads j.val and s.val+1, not only highest coefficients. To recover each 1<=s<=9 comparison from array equality, use Fin 9 value s-1; its bound and s-1+1=s are checked by omega. j<=n becomes j<n+1. The injective map domain is exactly the ProperMultiplier subtype, independently restated with the explicit inequality."
    },
    {
      "name": "quartic_all_n_original_integer_regime_and_zero_multiplier",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "Degree<=4 gives 2n+8<9(n+1) for every n>=0. Independent closed checks cover quartic array injection, n=0, and original Even n / n>=2 integer quartics via the injective Z-to-Q polynomial map. An independent theorem proves the zero multiplier remains proper for all n."
    },
    {
      "name": "strict_proper_boundary_and_essential_degree_condition",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "Independently compiled counterexamples: n=0,W=X^4 is proper, its actual coefficient at order s=1 is 1 and weightedR(t)=1/t for t!=0; it fails the two-degree-gap condition. For n=0,W=X^5 the multiplier is nonzero and not proper but every actual local coefficient vanishes. Thus strict properness permits simple poles and is essential for full-array injection; it does not establish rho1=0 or L convergence."
    },
    {
      "name": "full_array_only_and_formal_analytic_aggregate_boundary",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "This proves zero kernel and injection of the complete actual (n+1)*9 local coefficient array in the strict proper domain. It does not prove injection/inversion of the five aggregated zeta/constant outputs. Formal Q[[z]] coefficients are not numerical series evaluations. No global partial fractions, reflection/cancellation, denominator integrality, exact infinite L identity, prescribed output inverse, J certificate, or irrationality is supplied."
    }
